Subject: [PATCH] docs: name the guide line style fields and where grid opacity
 is set

---
 docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md       |  4 ++--
 docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md          | 14 ++++++++++----
 .../docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md   |  4 ++--
 .../docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md      | 14 ++++++++++----
 4 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md b/docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md
index ba81118..be2f053 100644
--- a/docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md
+++ b/docs/concepts/layout-axes-and-coordinates.md
@@ -175,8 +175,8 @@ const x = {
 | `reverse`         | Reverse the responsive range                             |
 
 Both grids default to hidden when `grid` is omitted. A style object enables
-the grid or baseline and accepts renderer-neutral stroke, opacity, width,
-dash, and line-cap fields.
+the grid or baseline and accepts renderer-neutral `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`,
+`strokeWidth`, `strokeDasharray`, and `lineCap` fields.
 
 Candidate generation and label layout are separate. Choose at most one of
 `axis.ticks.count`, `axis.ticks.spacing`, and `axis.ticks.values`. Grid lines
diff --git a/docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md b/docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md
index e323f94..a2abb8a 100644
--- a/docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md
+++ b/docs/reference/scales-guides-and-color.md
@@ -263,10 +263,16 @@ interface ChartAxisOptions<TValue extends ChartValue> {
 | `side`     | `bottom` for x; `left` for y | Places an x axis on top/bottom or a y axis on left/right.                |
 
 Set `grid` or `axis.line` to a `ChartGuideLineStyle` object to enable the
-guide and override its stroke, opacity, width, dash pattern, or line cap.
-Omitted style fields keep the normal theme defaults. An empty object is
-equivalent to `true`, and `axis.line` styles only the axis baseline, not its
-tick stubs. Use finite non-negative widths and opacity values from zero to one.
+guide and override its `stroke`, `strokeOpacity`, `strokeWidth`,
+`strokeDasharray`, or `lineCap`. Omitted style fields keep the normal theme
+defaults. An empty object is equivalent to `true`, and `axis.line` styles only
+the axis baseline, not its tick stubs. Use finite non-negative widths and
+opacity values from zero to one.
+
+The default grid opacity is set once on the grid group, and a style's
+`strokeOpacity` is written on each grid line, where it overrides the group. An
+SVG inspector therefore still shows the default on the group after an
+override.
 
 ```ts
 type ChartContinuousValue = number | Date
